Z||000004||KRMFiero||05-03-2001||07:52 AM||||I want one||||reg||1
Z||000005||Ken Wittlief||05-03-2001||08:55 AM||||There was a guy that put monstor tires on a dodge van, they were at least 3 feet in diameter and a foot and a half wide. I'd often see him pulling into the same gas station I used. Then one day I realized it was too much of a cooincidence. I had a dodge van at the time too, and I was getting about 15mpg city with the 308/auto.<P>  I asked him what kinda mileage he was getting. Then I knew why I saw him at the gas station almost everytime I was there.<P>  3mpg! with his 30 gallon tank he has a 100 mile range.<P>  and he used the vehicle for his contracting job. so he had to fillerup at least once a day.<P>  ouch!<P>  the reason doing this to a fireo is distastefull to many is cause we spend a lot of money to get the lightest wheel/tire combination possible. Having to spin those monster tires up to speed takes a huge amount of energy.<P>   so putting big heavy tires and wheels on a fiero would be... well, anti-fiero!||||reg||1
Z||000006||Ken Wittlief||05-03-2001||10:03 AM||||and besides, its just so,       unatural!<P>but it would warrent a cool name: <P> Fierostien<P>  Fierkenstien<P>    (ohmygod, Ive created a monster, It wasnt suppose to be like this, it was suppose to be a thing of beauty, what have I done?!)||||reg||1
